{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmSXakZFauUkh2rU3567","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The verdict is **MEANING for all three rows**. I re-anchored LLR-270 and TC-266. I did not approve SR-227's new text, so I sent it back to the authoring lane instead.\n\n**Verdict** (`cc1d6bda`, file `docs/reviews/wi-835-coordinator-retained-adjudication/002-ADJUDICATE-a10adc3.md`, ending `VERDICT: MEANING rows=3`):\n- **SR-227** (the Requirement and AcceptanceCriteria cells carry the change): retention now also covers adjudications the coordinator starts, not just the loop's. It adds a refusal when the dedicated home isn't signed in, and the acceptance gains a lane-worktree-only condition and a condition that the verdict must come from a call that finished within its deadline. An implementation correct under the old text fails all of these.\n- **LLR-270** (Detail): `plan_keep` now checks sign-in before `keep_for`, so a refused call takes no lease and creates no home. That is a new precondition and ordering.\n- **TC-266** (Method, Expected): it now asserts this repo's dial at 55 instead of 0, and drops the check that retention is off in this repo.\n\n**What I did after the verdict:**\n- **LLR-270 and TC-266 re-anchored** (`8c158b56`). I ran `intake.py snapshot --reattests LLR-270,TC-266 --verdict <verdict file>`; it was accepted and recorded as act 37. Only the LLR and TC registry copies changed. The new Drafted rows (LLR-305, TC-321 to TC-324) were copied in with the rest of those registries and are still marked Drafted.\n- **SR-227 returned, not re-anchored** (`eb061d2f`). Its acceptance now requires two things its Requirement never states: the lane-worktree-only condition and the in-deadline verdict condition. The Requirement only applies while the retention dial is on, but those two conditions apply to every coordinator adjudication whatever the dial says. I drafted the fix in a `## Dispositions` section of the WI-835 spec, and intake will mint it when WI-835 merges. The fix: either put both obligations into SR-227's Requirement and say they hold regardless of the dial, or move them to the SR that owns the coordinator entry point and update LLR-305's `sr_refs`. The draft parses cleanly with `intake.parse_dispositions`.\n- **SR-227 is still drifted.** `system-requirements.toml` keeps its old snapshot until the authoring lane answers the disposition and SR-227 is judged again.\n\nIn my first verdict commit a blank line separated `WI: WI-835` from Co-Authored-By, so git didn't read it as a trailer. I amended that unpushed commit, and all three commits now carry `WI: WI-835` as a trailer. I didn't change any registry cell."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1024,"cache_read_input_tokens":79378,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1024},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce1fccc0-8fec-4295-889e-541a0dc6f24a","uuid":"0b2d5614-5830-4131-9d23-de44854226c6","timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:16:29.707Z","request_id":"req_011CfmSXaM16NxutJvrnkPYp"}
